# APK on GitHub — latest only

## Hard rule

On GitHub Releases for this repo, **only one APK** may exist at a time: the **current latest** shell build.

- Tag pattern: `apk-X.Y.Z`
- Asset name: `SOS-X.Y.Z.apk`
- Mark that release as **Latest**
- After publishing the new APK, **delete** all older `apk-*` releases (and their assets/tags)

## Do not

- Leave previous APKs downloadable (causes UI to keep installing an old version)
- Point `NATIVE_APK_URL` / install UI at an older release while advertising a newer one
- Fall back from advertised version X to download URL for version Y

## When releasing a new APK

1. Upload `SOS-<new>.apk` to release `apk-<new>` with `--latest`
2. Update `apk-version.json` (`version`, `versionCode`, `file`, `url`, `published: true`)
3. Update `NATIVE_APK_VERSION` in `pwa-installer.js` to the same version
4. Delete every older `apk-*` release
5. Verify `gh release list` shows only the new tag as Latest with that single APK asset
